@startuml activity-flash-frame-parser
' Activity: how FlashFrameParser::consume() splits one serial byte stream
' into UART flash protocol frames and the telemetry text around them.
'
' Grounded in real source:
'   - src/integration/FlashFrameParser.h/.cpp  (consume, buffer_, falseStarts_)
'   - src/integration/FlashFrame.h/.cpp        (kFlashStartByte, kFlashMaxPayloadBytes,
'                                               crc16CcittFalse)
'   - docs/adr/0033-flash-frames-share-the-serial-link.md
'   - docs/protocols/uart-flash-v1.md          (section 3, section 9 item 8: resync)

title FlashFrameParser::consume - one stream, two kinds of traffic

skinparam shadowing false

start
:work = held bytes + new chunk;
while (bytes left at pos?) is (yes)
  if (byte at pos is 0xA5?) then (no)
    :append byte to **text**\n(telemetry, handed to SerialFrameParser);
    :pos += 1;
  else (yes)
    if (6-byte header complete?) then (no)
      :hold from pos, wait for next chunk;
      break
    endif
    if (LEN > 260?) then (yes)
      #Pink:false start: drop this 0xA5 only\nfalseStarts += 1\npos += 1;
    else (no)
      if (header + LEN + CRC complete?) then (no)
        :hold from pos, wait for next chunk;
        break
      endif
      if (CRC-16 matches?) then (no)
        #Pink:false start: drop this 0xA5 only\nfalseStarts += 1\npos += 1;
      else (yes)
        #PaleGreen:emit **frame** {type, seq, payload};
        :pos += whole frame;
      endif
    endif
  endif
endwhile (no)
:keep bytes from pos as buffer_\n(at most one unfinished frame);
stop

note right
  Resync never skips LEN bytes: a garbage LEN
  can reach 65535 and would swallow the real
  frames behind it. Scanning again from the next
  byte finds them at once.

  Text never contains 0xA5, so no mode switch is
  needed. A frame is read by LEN, so its payload
  may hold a newline or another 0xA5.
end note

@enduml
